{"id":"rus-t0-0015","lang":"rus","tier":0,"domain":3,"text_native":"Вы принимаете американские/австралийские/канадские доллары?","text_romanized":"vyh pree-nee-MAH-ee-tyeh uh-mee-ree-KAHN-skee-yeh / uhv-struh-LEE-skee-yeh / kuh-NAHD-skee-yeh DOH-luhr-yh","text_english":"Do you accept American/Australian/Canadian dollars?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking what something costs, and what you think of the price. Every transaction needs both.","caution":"Prices are often negotiable in a market and fixed in a shop. Asking what you think of it reads differently in each.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Russian phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Russian%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null,"corroborating_sentences":[],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
